WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:03.570
The Wizarding World is back with its newest
installment.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.870
Will there be beasts?

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:05.879
Will there be secrets?

00:00:05.879 --> 00:00:07.620
And will it all be fantastic?

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:11.820
Here’s what you need to know before you
see Fantastic Beasts: The Secrets of Dumbledore.”

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:16.500
Though "Fantastic Beasts: The Secrets of Dumbledore"
originally had a release date in the summer,

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.420
it's now set for release on April 15, 2022.

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:22.750
This puts the movie on track to debut just
in time for the Easter holiday.

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:26.980
According to Deadline, this particular opening
weekend has proven to be successful for Warner

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:31.600
Bros. in the past, with hits like "Batman
v Superman: Dawn of Justice" and "Ready Player

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.399
One" previously opening to big numbers during
that window.

00:00:34.399 --> 00:00:38.039
Both scheduled release dates were a change-up
from the November releases that the first

00:00:38.039 --> 00:00:39.710
two "Fantastic Beasts" films employed.

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:44.019
The new date may be an attempt to garner a
higher gross for the third film than its predecessors

00:00:44.019 --> 00:00:49.010
achieved; while the first movie grossed over
$814 million worldwide, the sequel brought

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:51.780
in less, at just over $654 million.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:56.000
A new release season may be an effort to trend
those returns back in the direction of the

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.420
blockbuster original "Harry Potter" movies.

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:02.469
Whatever the reasoning, it remains to be seen
if this move will pay off, but if past releases

00:01:02.469 --> 00:01:06.780
are any indication, Warner Bros. may be in
for a happy Easter.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:10.650
According to The Hollywood Reporter, "Fantastic
Beasts: The Secrets of Dumbledore" will pick

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:14.680
up sometime after the second film and continue
to follow Newt Scamander and his friends as

00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:15.950
they attempt to stop Grindelwald.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:18.579
"Who wouldn't like our chances?"

00:01:18.579 --> 00:01:22.250
According to an official synopsis for the
movie, "Professor Albus Dumbledore knows the

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:26.690
powerful Dark wizard Gellert Grindelwald is
moving to seize control of the wizarding world.

00:01:26.690 --> 00:01:31.869
Unable to stop him alone, he entrusts Magizoologist
Newt Scamander to lead an intrepid team of

00:01:31.869 --> 00:01:35.520
wizards, witches and one brave Muggle baker
on a dangerous mission, where they encounter

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:39.240
old and new beasts and clash with Grindelwald's
growing legion of followers.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:43.680
But with the stakes so high, how long can
Dumbledore remain on the sidelines?"

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:47.520
This synopsis, the film's title, and the trailers
indicate that Law's Dumbledore will play a

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:50.890
much bigger part in the movie than he did
previously, hopefully answering some of the

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:54.789
questions that fans have had for years about
the mysterious wizard.

00:01:54.789 --> 00:01:58.210
For fans who noticed a significant change
in Grindelwald's appearance from "The Crimes

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:01.229
of Grindelwald" to "The Secrets of Dumbledore,"
don't worry.

00:02:01.229 --> 00:02:05.409
Between flashback sequences, polyjuice potions,
and actor shake-ups, more than a few actors

00:02:05.409 --> 00:02:08.009
have played the ruthless dictator throughout
the years.

00:02:08.009 --> 00:02:11.470
Yet when "Fantastic Beasts and Where to Find
Them" first unmasked Johnny Depp's version

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:15.430
of the character, Depp seemed like the tried
and true version of this era's Grindelwald.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:19.610
However, Depp's ongoing legal battle with
ex-wife Amber Heard led to the studio's ultimate

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.300
decision to recast the role.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.300
But don't fret.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:26.170
Mads Mikkelsen is picking up where Depp left
off, and he's sporting an entirely different

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:27.550
look than his predecessor.

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:31.600
Depp's Grindelwald opted for bleach blond
hair and a pallor so gaunt he looked like

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.520
he came straight from the morgue.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.830
Mikkelsen's version of the character seems
much less eccentric — right down to the

00:02:36.830 --> 00:02:37.830
eyes.

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:41.660
If you look closely, it looks like Grindelwald's
signature heterochromia is still there, but

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.480
it's much less pronounced.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:47.590
Given that Grindelwald is taking his rise
to power to a political level, his stark appearance

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:51.210
change could be attributed to his need to
win over the wizarding population as he begins

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.850
his war on muggles.

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:54.290
As he says to Dumbledore,

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:56.630
"With or without you, I'll burn down their
world."

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:59.580
He just apparently needs his suit pressed
to do it.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:04.050
There may have been a few shakeups in "Fantastic
Beasts" casting, but the majority of the series'

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:08.400
staples from the franchise's first film will
return in "Fantastic Beasts: The Secrets of

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:09.400
Dumbledore."

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:13.230
Of course, there's no "Fantastic Beasts" without
magizoologist Newt Scamander.

00:03:13.230 --> 00:03:17.890
Eddie Redmayne plays Newt, the wizarding world's
most notorious (and relatable) Hufflepuff.

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:21.400
Meanwhile, given that the film is titled "The
Secrets of Dumbledore," it's no surprise that

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.570
Jude Law is reprising his role as the much
younger Dumbledore.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:29.310
Also returning is Jacob, the series' main
source of comic relief, played by Dan Fogler.

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:33.370
If the trailers are anything to go by, fans
are getting a healthy dose of Jacob-centric

00:03:33.370 --> 00:03:34.560
laughs in the upcoming movie.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.790
Though with a new wand in tow, the wizarding
world's most notorious No-Maj just might be

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:40.470
a No-Maj no more.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:44.500
As much as fans love the heroes, the villains
are equally exciting for a franchise like

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:45.730
"Fantastic Beasts."

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:49.850
Queenie's descent to Grindelwald's side was
a shock for most fans, but the trailer poses

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:54.040
a few epic villainous moments for her, expertly
carried out by Alison Sudol.

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:57.590
And who could forget Ezra Miller's electric
performance as Credence Barebone as he works

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:00.480
through his trauma while toting an Obscurus?

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:04.160
Grindelwald may be the main show here, but
his lackeys hold their own just fine.

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:08.730
"The Crimes of Grindelwald" introduced fans
to Newt's auror brother Theseus Scamander,

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:12.850
but the new film's trailers imply that Callum
Turner will play a much more significant role

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:15.180
in the quest to take down Grindelwald.

00:04:15.180 --> 00:04:18.970
Joining the anti-Grindelwald movement in what
seems like a big way is Jessica Williams'

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:23.310
Ilvermorny charms professor Eulalie Hicks,
following up on her introduction in "The Crimes

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:24.310
of Grindelwald."

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:28.370
And, of course, a trip to Hogwarts wouldn't
be right without a cameo from a young Minerva

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:31.910
McGonagall, who alerts Dumbledore to Grindelwald's
plans.

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:35.720
Fans didn't get many scenes with Newt's "Crimes
of Grindelwald" assistant Bunty, but it looks

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:39.990
like actress Victoria Yeates is returning
for the third film, and the trailer is positioning

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:43.560
her as a soldier in Dumbledore's first army
against Grindelwald.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:48.120
Poppy Corby-Tuech is also coming back to the
third "Fantastic Beasts" film as Vinda, ready

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:51.090
to fight for Grindelwald with everything she's
got.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:54.930
Alternatively, William Nadylam's Yusuf Kama
may have had a rocky start in "The Crimes

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:59.870
of Grindelwald," but Leta Lestrange's half-brother
quickly goes from a pseudo-villain to a hero,

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:02.490
spurning Grindelwald's invitation and saving
Nagini.

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:07.420
Though Leta herself met an untimely demise,
Yusuf will be back in "The Secrets of Dumbledore"

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:08.420
to carry on her legacy.

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:13.210
For anyone who hasn't seen "Harry Potter and
the Half-Blood Prince" in a minute, Michael

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:16.631
Gambon's appearance in the second "Fantastic
Beasts: The Secrets of Dumbledore" trailer

00:05:16.631 --> 00:05:18.430
may have come as an exciting shock.

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:20.930
However, his cameo is a bit of a bait-and-switch.

00:05:20.930 --> 00:05:25.180
While the trailer implies that we may see
an aged-up Dumbledore grace our screens once

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:28.800
more, the clip is just recycled footage from
the sixth "Harry Potter" film.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.670
"That's why he's returning to Hogwarts.

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:33.310
And it's crucial he should return."

00:05:33.310 --> 00:05:36.530
The trailer starts with Gambon saying, "Memory
is everything.

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:37.980
Without it, we are blind.

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:40.630
Without it, we leave the fate of our world
to chance."

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:44.520
Of course, this snippet is simply an edited-down
version of Dumbledore's speech to Harry when

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:48.660
he takes the teenage wizard on a trip down
Tom Riddle's memory lane through his Pensieve.

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:52.431
Still, repurposed footage or not, the trailer
raised the question – is Michael Gambon

00:05:52.431 --> 00:05:55.550
returning to the wizarding world in "The Secrets
of Dumbledore"?

00:05:55.550 --> 00:05:56.669
That's doubtful.

00:05:56.669 --> 00:06:00.650
As far as we can tell, it's only in the trailer
for the sake of nostalgia – and grabbing

00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:01.680
your attention.

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:05.200
Stranger things have happened in the wizarding
world, but as a different Dumbledore once

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:06.200
said:

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:12.650
"It does not do to dwell on dreams and forget
to live."

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:17.140
The "Fantastic Beasts: The Secrets of Dumbledore"
title sets fans up with serious expectations

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:19.310
in diving into Dumbledore's backstory.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:22.169
According to Entertainment Weekly, back in
2007, J.K.

00:06:22.169 --> 00:06:26.050
Rowling announced that she "always thought
of Dumbledore as gay" and envisioned a relationship

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:31.300
between the Hogwarts headmaster and Grindelwald
– yet the books barely hint at this plotline.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:35.270
Given that we've gone through two movies that
specifically revolve around young Dumbledore

00:06:35.270 --> 00:06:38.810
and Grindelwald, it's been frustrating for
fans to again rely on subtle clues rather

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:41.919
than concrete scenes or conversations detailing
this relationship.

00:06:41.919 --> 00:06:46.800
However, we do see the former friends and
possible lovers square off in the trailer,

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:49.980
implying that Dumbledore broke his no-fighting
blood pact with Grindelwald.

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:54.320
Hopefully, fans will also get clarity on the
pair's history and relationship when they

00:06:54.320 --> 00:06:55.320
spar.

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:58.150
Like his sexuality, Dumbledore keeps his family
history close to the vest.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:02.770
However, Hebe Beardsall is returning as Albus
and Aberforth's sister Ariana, and joining

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:06.090
her is Richard Coyle taking on the role of
Albus' brother.

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:10.260
Maybe fans will get answers on what happened
between Aberforth, Ariana, Albus, and Grindelwald

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:11.669
all those years ago.

00:07:11.669 --> 00:07:15.230
Presumably fans are more interested in this
history than Harry Potter was.

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:17.910
“I’m not interested in what happened between
you and your brother.”

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:22.290
Though because the trailer teases a big Room
of Requirement moment, Ariana and Aberforth's

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:25.280
cameos might be as superficial as they were
in the “Deathly Hallows.”

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:29.240
It looks like Aberforth is already running
the Hog's Head Inn, while Ariana has long

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:33.480
since passed — making it likely that she'll
resume her role as a portrait guide rather

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:35.910
than a developed character.

00:07:35.910 --> 00:07:39.820
There can't be a "Fantastic Beasts" movie
without some fantastic beasts, and it looks

00:07:39.820 --> 00:07:42.710
like "The Secrets of Dumbledore" is prepared
to deliver.

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:46.371
Not only do the trailers feature some beloved
creatures like Pickett the Bowtruckle, but

00:07:46.371 --> 00:07:49.070
we finally have a name for Newt's trusty Niffler.

00:07:49.070 --> 00:07:52.740
Another major beast to make its way into the
trailer is Credence's phoenix — lending

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:54.840
more credence to him being a Dumbledore.

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:59.050
Now, it certainly wouldn't be surprising for
this to be a red herring, but it's equally

00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:02.770
possible that there's even more murky family
history surrounding the Dumbledore name than

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:04.060
fans initially thought.

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:08.830
In fact, the title says "The Secrets of Dumbledore,"
not "The Secrets of Albus Dumbledore."

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:13.180
There's a very real possibility that the title
is pointing to the secrets of another Dumbledore

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.370
entirely.

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:17.530
Outside of Credence, there are at least two
other Dumbledores in the movie.

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:19.940
Presumably they all have some secrets.

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:23.630
On top of the beasts we have names for, the
trailer depicts a new kind of magical bird,

00:08:23.630 --> 00:08:26.600
crab creatures, and a shadowy group of stingers.

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:30.540
All in all, the movie isn't shaping up to
disappoint on creature comforts.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:33.809
As famed wandmaker Garrick Ollivander likes
to say,

00:08:33.809 --> 00:08:36.689
“The wand chooses the wizard, Mr. Potter.”

00:08:36.689 --> 00:08:41.029
But for a wand to choose a wizard, the wielder
must be an actual wizard, right?

00:08:41.029 --> 00:08:44.850
If you ask any Squib, they'll probably tell
you that a wand on its own doesn't wield all

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:47.560
that much power — it's just a tool, after
all.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:51.529
Sure, some wands are more potent than others,
but then again, some witches and wizards are

00:08:51.529 --> 00:08:54.350
more powerful than others, and wands choose
their match.

00:08:54.350 --> 00:08:58.769
So, how is it that No-Maj Jacob is wielding
a wand in "Fantastic Beasts: The Secrets of

00:08:58.769 --> 00:08:59.809
Dumbledore"?

00:08:59.809 --> 00:09:03.440
In the second "Fantastic Beasts: The Secrets
of Dumbledore" trailer, Dumbledore asks Newt

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:04.629
to give Jacob a wand.

00:09:04.629 --> 00:09:07.050
Could there be magic in Jacob after all?

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:10.999
There might be a reason why the wizards let
a muggle tag along on their quests for years

00:09:10.999 --> 00:09:15.100
— and an explanation for how he breaks through
a memory wipe.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:18.779
There are quite a few significant characters
from the "Fantastic Beasts" films whose stories

00:09:18.779 --> 00:09:21.890
are currently hanging in plot limbo, waiting
for a revival.

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:25.639
It's certainly possible that some of the seemingly
missing cast members and characters might

00:09:25.639 --> 00:09:29.610
show up anyway, but based on available info,
it doesn’t seem likely.

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:34.200
Most notably absent is Claudia Kim, who plays
the human iteration of Voldemort's snake Nagini.

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:38.320
"Crimes of Grindelwald '' faced a significant
amount of backlash for setting the groundwork

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:42.610
for Voldemort to essentially enslave an Asian
woman — and then later encase a portion

00:09:42.610 --> 00:09:44.569
of his warped soul inside of her.

00:09:44.569 --> 00:09:48.670
Whether Nagini's absence is due to the backlash
against the character, her casting, or because

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:52.829
her arc with Credence is over, it doesn't
look like Nagini will be slithering back for

00:09:52.829 --> 00:09:54.459
the newest film.

00:09:54.459 --> 00:09:58.180
One significant change from the previous films
that fans may not have noticed has nothing

00:09:58.180 --> 00:09:59.610
to do with the cast.

00:09:59.610 --> 00:10:02.800
In the first two "Fantastic Beasts" films,
"Harry Potter" author J.K.

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:06.279
Rowling retained sole writing and screenwriting
credits for both movies.

00:10:06.279 --> 00:10:10.730
Yet in "Fantastic Beasts: The Secrets of Dumbledore,"
fans may recognize a familiar writing credit

00:10:10.730 --> 00:10:13.649
on IMDb: Steve Kloves.

00:10:13.649 --> 00:10:17.430
Kloves was responsible for writing seven of
the eight "Harry Potter" films, and now it

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:21.550
looks like Kloves is back on his broomstick
to assist in writing the newest "Fantastic

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:22.550
Beasts" installment.

00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:25.829
The real reason for the assist is unknown,
but it could have something to do with the

00:10:25.829 --> 00:10:30.179
studio trying to minimize Rowling’s involvement
with the film in light of her recent transphobic

00:10:30.179 --> 00:10:31.179
statements.

00:10:31.179 --> 00:10:33.420
Or, it’s possible, she just didn’t want
to write the movie solo.

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:37.269
Regardless, the movie will see yet another
returning Harry Potter veteran behind the

00:10:37.269 --> 00:10:40.480
camera besides Kloves: director David Yates.

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:44.339
Yates is a "Potter" staple, having directed
"The Order of the Phoenix" through "Deathly

00:10:44.339 --> 00:10:48.529
Hallows: Part 2" and continuing his reign
through the first two "Fantastic Beasts" films.

00:10:48.529 --> 00:10:52.089
The director returns for "Fantastic Beasts:
The Secrets of Dumbledore" to add a level

00:10:52.089 --> 00:10:55.959
of continuity that's rare for a franchise
so massive.

00:10:55.959 --> 00:10:58.260
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:02.910
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies and TV shows are coming soon.

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:06.609
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

